PS3: keep libsupc++'s exception state in thread-local storage.

libstdc++ checks for TLS support (GCC_CHECK_TLS) only in its native
configuration.  The --with-newlib cross branch used for the PS3 skips the
check, so _GLIBCXX_HAVE_TLS stayed undefined and eh_globals.cc fell back
to one static __cxa_eh_globals object (the caught-exception stack and the
uncaught count) shared by every PPU thread.  Two threads inside exception
handling at once then saw each other's exceptions.

Lv-2 gives each PPU thread its own TLS block (r13), and PPU __thread
storage is already used by the SDK, so define HAVE_TLS for
powerpc64-ps3-elf in the newlib branch.  eh_globals.cc then keeps
__cxa_eh_globals in __thread storage, one per thread.  The thread model
stays single; the other libgcc/libstdc++ locks are unchanged.

The generated configure is edited by hand in the same place, as in patch
0036.  Checked against Autoconf 2.69 (the version GCC 12.4 pins): the lines
autoconf adds to configure for this configure.ac change are byte-identical
to the hand edit.  A full regeneration does not reproduce the shipped
configure even without this change, because patch 0006's PS3 case in
crossconfig.m4 was never regenerated into configure; that branch only runs
without --with-newlib, which the PS3 build always passes.

--- a/libstdc++-v3/configure.ac
+++ b/libstdc++-v3/configure.ac
@@ -330,6 +330,14 @@
   # on a hosted environment.
   if test "x${with_newlib}" = "xyes"; then
     os_include_dir="os/newlib"
+    # PS3: each PPU thread gets its own TLS block from Lv-2, so keep
+    # libsupc++'s exception state (eh_globals) in __thread storage.
+    # This branch skips GCC_CHECK_TLS, which only runs natively.
+    case "${host}" in
+      powerpc64-ps3-elf*)
+        AC_DEFINE(HAVE_TLS)
+        ;;
+    esac
     AC_DEFINE(HAVE_HYPOT)
 
     # GLIBCXX_CHECK_STDLIB_SUPPORT
--- a/libstdc++-v3/configure
+++ b/libstdc++-v3/configure
@@ -29197,6 +29197,15 @@
   # on a hosted environment.
   if test "x${with_newlib}" = "xyes"; then
     os_include_dir="os/newlib"
+    # PS3: each PPU thread gets its own TLS block from Lv-2, so keep
+    # libsupc++'s exception state (eh_globals) in __thread storage.
+    # This branch skips GCC_CHECK_TLS, which only runs natively.
+    case "${host}" in
+      powerpc64-ps3-elf*)
+        $as_echo "#define HAVE_TLS 1" >>confdefs.h
+
+        ;;
+    esac
     $as_echo "#define HAVE_HYPOT 1" >>confdefs.h
 
 
